   "answer": "In AWS, audit records are shipped to CloudWatch Logs and archived to S3 with Object Lock for immutable retention. [1] Arguments can be stored as a hash so the audit trail does not become a second copy of sensitive data. [2] Chaining each record to the hash of the previous record makes the log tamper-evident: editing or deleting any record breaks every hash that follows. [3]",
